ContextOS database migrations (Alembic). The schema is owned by these revisions: production never
creates tables from the models, and the API refuses to start until the database is at the latest
revision (app/database/migrations.py).

Apply (from backend/):
    .venv/bin/python -m app.cli init-db          # = contextos-server init-db, or `make migrate`
The database URL is CONTEXTOS_DATABASE_URL (alembic.ini's sqlalchemy.url is not used); plain alembic
commands work too: `.venv/bin/alembic upgrade head`, or `.venv/bin/alembic -x url=<url> upgrade head`.

Write a revision after changing app/models (never against backend/data/contextos.db):
    export CONTEXTOS_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////tmp/<scratch>/m.db
    .venv/bin/alembic upgrade head
    .venv/bin/alembic revision --autogenerate -m "<what changed>"
Then review the file by hand:
  - no application imports: use sa.DateTime(timezone=True) (env.py renders UTCDateTime that way) and
    sa.JSON().with_variant(postgresql.JSONB(astext_type=sa.Text()), "postgresql") for JSON;
  - keep op.batch_alter_table(...) blocks for ALTERs (SQLite); name every constraint;
  - a new NOT NULL column on a populated table needs a server_default or a backfill;
  - write a real downgrade().
Verify on a fresh SQLite file and on a scratch PostgreSQL 17 (initdb/pg_ctl on a port in 18000-18999):
    .venv/bin/alembic upgrade head && .venv/bin/alembic check
    .venv/bin/alembic downgrade -1 && .venv/bin/alembic upgrade head
and run tests/integration/test_migrations.py.
